This error is occurring because app.router is deprecated in newer versions of Express.

In Express v4.x and below, app.router was used to enable the built-in router middleware.

However, in Express v5.0.0 and above, the router middleware is enabled by default - so app.router is no longer needed and has been deprecated.

To fix this error, you simply need to remove the app.use(app.router) line from your Express app.

For example:

Express v4 (uses app.router):
```js
const express = require('express')
const app = express()

app.use(app.router) 

app.get('/about', (req, res) => {
  res.send('About page')
})
```

Express v5 (no need for app.router):
```js 
const express = require('express')
const app = express()

app.get('/about', (req, res) => {
  res.send('About page')
})
```

So in modern Express apps, you can simply remove any instances of app.use(app.router) and the router middleware will still be enabled, avoiding the deprecation warning.

