```javascript
function quickSort(array) {
    if (array.length <= 1) {
        return array;
    }

    const pivot = array[0];
    const less = [...array.slice(1)];
    const greater = [...array.slice(1)];

    less = quickSort(less);
    greater = quickSort(greater);

    return [...less, pivot, ...greater];
}
```
This implementation uses the "pivot" element as the pivot point to partition the array into two sub-arrays, "less" and "greater", based on whether the element is less than or greater than the pivot. Then, it recursively sorts both sub-arrays using the quicksort algorithm. Finally, it concatenates the sorted sub-arrays with the pivot element to produce the final sorted array.

