`pm2 start ecosystem.config.js --config /path/to/ecosystem.config.js`

The ecosystem config file exports an object with apps and deploy keys:

```js
module.exports = {
  apps : [
    // app definitions
  ],
  deploy : {
    // deployment definitions
  }
}
```

So a very basic example would be:

```js
module.exports = {
  apps : [
    {
      name: "app",
      script: "app.js"
    }
  ]
}
```

This will run `app.js` and name the process `app`.

The ecosystem config allows you to define multiple apps to run and manage, as well as deployment configurations to facilitate zero-downtime deployments.

