A `switch` statement is a standard language construct in C and C++ used for conditional statements. It allows you to execute different blocks of code based on the value of an expression. The basic syntax of a `switch` statement is:
```php
switch (expression) {
   case value1:
      // code to execute if expression matches value1
      break;
   case value2:
      // code to execute if expression matches value2
      break;
   //...
   default:
      // code to execute if expression does not match any of the values
      break;
}
```
