Yes, `GCHandle` is a class in C# that provides a way to pin objects to memory, which can help prevent them from being garbage collected and recreated.

When an object is pinned, the .NET runtime is not allowed to reclaim the memory used by that object, even if it is no longer needed. This can be useful in situations where you have large objects that are frequently created and destroyed, and you want to minimize the amount of memory used by your application.

Here is an example of how you can use `GCHandle` to pin an object to memory:
```csharp
// Create an instance of MyClass
