    config.readConfig();

    // Use the configuration values
    std::cout << config.get("some

key") << std::endl;

config.writeConfig();

return 0;
}
```
4. Finally, you will need to add code to your application that creates the flat file configuration file and writes the configuration values to it when the application starts. You can also add code that reads the configuration file and loads the configuration values into the configuration class when the application starts.
```c++
int main() {
    // create the config file if it doesn't exist
    if (!Config("config.txt").exists()) {
        Config("config.txt").writeConfig();
    }

    // read the config file and load the configuration values into the config class
    Config config("config.txt");
    config.readConfig();

    // Use the configuration values
    std::cout << config.get("some key") << std::endl;

    // write the configuration values back to the config file
    config.writeConfig();

return 0;
}
```
