Copy code

struct S {
void f(int) {} // non-template

template <class T>
void f(T) {}   // template
};
Is there a way to detect on compile time that call of f(int) would be a normal member function, not a template function? Something like this is_template_v<S::f(int)> == false.

In case of absence regular member function void f(int) the check above should return true.

