Here is a Perl script that lists all PDF files on the server and deletes them all:

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use warnings;
use File::Find;

my $dir = '/path/to/directory/containing/pdfs';
find($dir) or die "find: $?";

while (my $file = file()) {
    if ($file =~ /\.pdf$/) {
        unlink($file) or die "unlink: $?";
    }
}
```

This script uses the `find` function to search for all files with the.pdf extension in the specified directory. The `file` function is then used to get the next file, and the `unlink` function is used to delete the file. The script will only delete files that are in the specified directory and have the.pdf extension.

