```javascript
function sortArray(arr: any[]) {
  let temp: any;
  let sorted: any[] = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {
      if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
        // swap elements
        temp = arr[j];
        arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
        arr[j + 1] = temp;

        // update the sorted array
        sorted.push(arr[j]);
      }
    }
  }

  return sorted;
}
```
This algorithm is called the "bubble sort" algorithm, and it works by repeatedly iterating over the array and comparing adjacent elements. If an element is larger than the next element in the array, the two elements are swapped. The algorithm continues until the array is sorted.

