double GetChance(int daysPassed)
{
    double chance;
    if (daysPassed == 0)
    {
        chance = 0;
    }
    else
    {
        chance = (daysPassed / 15) * 100;
    }
    return chance;
}
```
This function takes an integer `daysPassed` as input and returns a double value between 0 and 100. If no days have passed, it sets the chance to 0. Otherwise, it calculates the chance by taking the number of days passed divided by 15 and multiplying it by 100. This results in the chance increasing linearly as more days pass.

