In NAME_1, object pooling can be implemented using the UnityEngine.ObjectPool class. This class provides a simple way to create and manage a pool of objects that can be reused as needed. The ObjectPool class automatically handles the allocation and deallocation of objects, as well as the management of the pool's size and the objects' lifetimes.
To use the ObjectPool class, you first need to create a pool of objects with the desired initial size. Then, you can request an object from the pool and use it as needed. When you're done with the object, you should return it to the pool so that it can be reused by another object. When the pool's size falls below a certain threshold, the ObjectPool class will automatically create new objects to replenish the pool.
