Here are 3 ways to undo the express.json() middleware:

1. Call app.use(express.json(), null) - This will remove the middleware from the stack.

```js
app.use(express.json());

// Later...
app.use(express.json(), null);
```

2. Use app.disable('json parser') - This will disable the middleware.

```js 
app.use(express.json());

// Later...
app.disable('json parser');
```

3. Remove the middleware function directly from app.middlewares - This bypasses Express's middleware management.

```js
app.use(express.json());

// Later...
app.middlewares.splice(app.middlewares.indexOf(express.json), 1);
```

So in summary, you can either:

- Call the middleware again with null as the second argument
- Disable the middleware name 
- Directly remove the middleware function from app.middlewares

