To generate an OpenMP program that scales well, we can use a parallel loop with a large number of iterations. We can use the `+` operator to add the values of an array instead of using a for loop. Here is an example code:
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <omp.h>

int main() {
    int a[100000];
    #pragma omp parallel for
    for (int i = 0; i < 100000; ++i) {
        a[i] = i * 2;
    }
    return 0;
}
```
