    var fileContent = File.ReadAllText("path/to/file.txt");

    // Do something with the data, such as writing it to a file or storing it in a database
    //...
});

thread.Start();
```
This code creates a new thread and calls the `Start` method to start the thread. The thread then begins running and performs the file loading task.

Note that the `Start` method must be called on a thread that has the `IsBackground` property set to `false`. If the thread is already running, the `Start` method will not start a new instance of the thread. You can also use the `Join` method to wait for the thread to complete its task before returning from the method.

