  a: [b, c],
  b: [a, d],
  c: [a],
  d: [b]
};

bfs(graph, 'a');
```
This will traverse the graph starting from node 'a' and visit all the nodes in the graph.

Please note that this is a basic implementation and there are many optimizations and variations of the BFS algorithm that you can use depending on your specific use case.

