Here's a ts-node script that uses terraformer to reverse terraform all active resources in an AWS account:

```ts
import { Terraformer } from 'terraformer';
import { AWS } from 'aws-sdk';

const aws = new AWS();
const terraformer = new Terraformer();

async function main() {
  const regions = await aws.EC2.describeRegions().promise();
  const regionNames = regions.Regions.map(r => r.RegionName);

  for (const regionName of regionNames) {
    const resources = await terraformer.listResources({
      aws: {
        region: regionName
      }
    });

    for (const resource of resources) {
      if (resource.active) {
        console.log(`Reversing ${resource.type} ${resource.name} in ${regionName}`);
        await terraformer.reverseResource({
          aws: {
            region: regionName
          },
          resource
        });
      }
    }
  }
}

main();
```

This script:

- Gets all AWS regions using the AWS SDK
- For each region, lists all resources using terraformer
- Checks if each resource is active
- If so, reverses that resource using terraformer, effectively deleting it
- This has the effect of reversing all active AWS resources in the account.

