Here's a JavaScript function that uses a regular expression to prevent the user from entering a decimal number in an input HTML element:
```javascript
function preventDecimalInput(inputElement) {
  const regex = /^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$/; // regular expression to match decimal numbers
  const inputValue = inputElement.value;
  if (regex.test(inputValue)) {
    // if the input value matches the regular expression, prevent the user from submitting the form
    inputElement.setAttribute('onsubmit', function(event) {
      event.preventDefault();
      alert('Please enter a whole number without decimals.');
    });
  } else {
    // if the input value does not match the regular expression, remove the onsubmit attribute
    inputElement.removeAttribute('onsubmit');
  }
}
```
To use this function, you can pass in the input element that you want to apply the regular expression to, like this:
```html
<input type="text" id="myInput" onsubmit="preventDecimalInput(this)">
```
This will prevent the user from submitting the form if they enter a decimal number in the input element.

