Here's a simple C++ program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file:


```javascript
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

int main() {
    ifstream file("example.txt", ios::in); // open the file in input mode
    if (!file.is_open()) {
        return 1;
    }

    int lineNumber = 1; // start counting from the first line
    int wordCount = 0;

    while (getline(file, line[lineNumber], '\n')) {
        for (auto word : line[lineNumber]) {
            if (word == "word") {
                wordCount++;
            }
        }
        lineNumber++;
    }

    file.close();

    cout << "Count of word: " << wordCount << endl;

    return 0;
}

```

In this program, we use the `` ifstream `` class to open the file in input mode. We then set the starting line number to 1 and initialize the variable `` wordCount `` to 0.

The `` while `` loop reads each line of the file using the `` getline() `` function, which extracts the characters of the line, including the newline character at the end of the line. We then loop through each character in the line and check if it is equal to the word "word". If it is, we increment `` wordCount ``.

After the loop is finished, we close the file. The final output of the program is the count of the word "word" in the file, which is stored in the `` wordCount `` variable.

public class CacheUtil<K, V> {
    private long DEFAULT_EXPIRATION_TIME = 60L * 1000;

    private Map<K, CacheItem<V>> cacheMap = new HashMap<>();

    public void put(K key, V value) {
        put(key, value, DEFAULT_EXPIRATION_TIME);
    }

    public void put(K key, V value, long expirationTime) {
        long expiration = System.currentTimeMillis() + expirationTime;
        cacheMap.put(key, new CacheItem<V>(value, expiration));
    }

    public V get(K key) {
        CacheItem<V> cacheItem = cacheMap.get(key);
        if (cacheItem == null) {
            return null;
        }
        if (System.currentTimeMillis() > cacheItem.getExpiration()) {
            cacheMap.remove(key);
            return null;
        }
        return cacheItem.getValue();
    }

    public int size() {
        return cacheMap.size();
    }

