fix bugs in this php code

usort($hours, function ($x, $y) {
			if ($x['date'] === $y['date']) {
				return strcmp($x['name'], $y['name']);
			}
			return $x['date'] >= $y['date'];
		});

Here are a few issues I see in this code:

1. The comparison function passed to usort() should return -1, 0 or 1, not booleans. It should be:

```php
usort($hours, function ($x, $y) {
			if ($x['date'] === $y['date']) {
				return strcmp($x['name'], $y['name']);
			}
			return $x['date'] <=> $y['date'];
		});
```

2. Using === to compare dates is not a good idea. It will do a strict comparison and fail if the dates are not exactly the same object. It should be:

```php
usort($hours, function ($x, $y) {
			if ($x['date'] == $y['date']) {
				return strcmp($x['name'], $y['name']);
			}
			return $x['date'] <=> $y['date'];
		});
```

3. strcmp() will do a case-sensitive comparison. It may be better to use strcasecmp() for case-insensitive comparison of names.

4. The code does not have any error handling. It will fail if $hours is not an array or does not contain 'date' and 'name' keys. It should have checks like:

```php 
if (!is_array($hours) || !isset($hours[0]['date']) || !isset($hours[0]['name'])) {
    return false;
}
```

So the fixed code would be:

```php
if (!is_array($hours) || !isset($hours[0]['date']) || !isset($hours[0]['name'])) {
