In CodeIgniter, you can redirect from one controller method to another using the redirect() function. For example:

```php
public function method1()
{
    $this->redirect('controller2/method2');
}
```

This will redirect from method1 of the current controller to method2 of the controller2 controller.

The redirect() function accepts two parameters:

1. The URL to redirect to. This can be a string as shown above, or an array.
2. The HTTP redirect status code. By default it is 302 (Found). You can use 301 (Permanent Redirect) or other codes if needed.

So a full example would be:

```php
public function method1()
{
    $this->redirect('controller2/method2', 301);
}
```

This will perform a 301 permanent redirect from method1 to method2.

The URL you pass to redirect() can also be an array, for example:

```php
$url = [
    'controller' => 'controller2',
    'method'     => 'method2'
];
$this->redirect($url);
```

This has the same effect of redirecting to controller2/method2.

