```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class AsyncReaderWriterLock
{
    private readonly SemaphoreSlim _semaphore = new SemaphoreSlim(1, 1);
    private readonly TaskCompletionSource<object> _waitTask = new TaskCompletionSource<object>();

    public async Task WaitAsync()
    {
        await _waitTask.Task;
    }

    public async Task ReadAsync()
    {
        await _semaphore.WaitAsync(CancellationToken.None);
        Console.WriteLine("Reader acquired");
    }

    public async Task WriteAsync()
    {
        await _semaphore.WaitAsync(CancellationToken.None);
        Console.WriteLine("Writer acquired");
    }

    public async Task ReleaseReadAsync()
    {
        await _semaphore.ReleaseAsync();
        Console.WriteLine("Reader released");
    }

    public async Task ReleaseWriteAsync()
    {
        await _semaphore.ReleaseAsync();
        Console.WriteLine("Writer released");
    }
}
```
In this implementation, the `SemaphoreSlim` class is used to provide asynchronous semaphore functionality. The `WaitAsync` method waits for the semaphore to become available, and the `ReadAsync` and `WriteAsync` methods acquire the semaphore and perform the read or write operation. The `ReleaseReadAsync` and `ReleaseWriteAsync` methods release the semaphore when they are no longer needed.

The `TaskCompletionSource` class is used to provide a way to complete the `WaitAsync` method when the semaphore becomes available. When the semaphore is acquired, the continuation passed to the `WaitAsync` method is executed, which prints a message to the console indicating that the operation has completed.

