For the Azure Translator API, the Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Region header specifies the region that your subscription is tied to.
So in your case, since your region is North Europe, you should set the header value to:

Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Region: northeurope

So your full code would be:
```csharp
public async Task<string> TranslateAsync(string fromLanguage, string toLanguage, string text)
{
    var route = $"/translate?api-version=3.0&from={fromLanguage}&to={toLanguage}";
    var body = new object[] { new { Text = text } };
    var requestBody = JsonSerializer.Serialize(body);

    var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, route)
    {
        Content = new StringContent(requestBody, Encoding.UTF8, "application/json")
    };
    request.Headers.Add("Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key", httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders["Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key"]);
    request.Headers.Add("Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Region", "northeurope");

    var response = await httpClient.SendAsync(request); 

    response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
    var result = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();
    return result;
}
```

Adding that header will ensure your requests are routed to the North Europe region for your subscription.
