```c
dlclose(my_lib);
```
After this call, the `libmylibrary.so` library will be unloaded, and its symbols, including `my_function`, will be removed from the address space of your application.

Keep in mind that unloading a shared library can cause issues if other parts of your application or other libraries are still using its symbols. Make sure to call `dlclose()` only when you're certain that no other code needs the library's symbols anymore.

