If you want to execute code on the server whenever a RepNotify message is sent, you can override the default behavior by setting the bServerHandler flag to true in the RepNotify system. This will cause the RepNotify message to be executed on the server instead of the client.

Here is an example of how you can set the bServerHandler flag to true in your RepNotify system:
```kotlin
void BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    // Enable RepNotify system and set bServerHandler flag to true
    AddEBeginPlayOverlay("RepNotify System");
    RepNotify.SetEnabled(true);
    RepNotify.SetServerHandler(true);
}
```
In this example, we are enabling the RepNotify system and setting the bServerHandler flag to true in the BeginPlay method. This will cause any RepNotify messages sent from the client to be executed on the server.

Note that if you are using custom logic in your RepNotify system, you will need to ensure that the logic is executed on the server as well. You can do this by creating a custom RepNotify system that inherits from the URepNotifySystem class, and overriding the OnRepNotifyMessage function to execute your custom logic on the server.

