Here is a C# method that calculates the variance and standard deviation of a list of doubles:

```csharp
public void CalculateVarianceAndStdDev(List<double> numbers)
{
    double sum = 0;
    double sumOfSquares = 0;

    foreach (double num in numbers)
    {
        sum += num;
        sumOfSquares += num * num;
    }

    int n = numbers.Count;
    double mean = sum / n;
    double variance = (sumOfSquares - sum * sum / n) / (n - 1);
    double stdDev = Math.Sqrt(variance);

    Console.WriteLine($"Mean: {mean}");
    Console.WriteLine($"Variance: {variance}");
    Console.WriteLine($"Standard Deviation: {stdDev}");
}
```

This method does the following:

- Calculates the sum and sum of squares of the numbers
- Calculates the mean by dividing the sum by the count
- Calculates the variance by dividing the sum of squares minus the sum squared divided by count, divided by count minus one
- Takes the square root of the variance to get the standard deviation
- Prints the mean, variance and standard deviation

